\f1\b0 \cf2 \cb4 Official Review\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 by\'a0Reviewer 5qN309 May 2026, 00:48 (modified: 22 May 2026, 06:48)Program Chairs, Area Chairs, Reviewers Submitted, Authors, Reviewer 5qN3{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://openreview.net/revisions?id=TnIywE3qCH"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \strokec6 Revisions}}\cf7 \cb1 \strokec7 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf8 \cb3 \strokec8 Summary:
\f1\b0 \cf7 \cb1 \strokec7 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf7 \cb3 The core idea of this paper is that, in Transformer attention, Query-Key mainly serves to \'93select\'94 relevant tokens, while Value is responsible for \'93transferring\'94 full representations. Therefore, the dimensionality of Key/Query does not necessarily need to be the same as that of Value. The experiments cover small-scale algorithmic tasks, post-training compression of GPT-2, training from scratch at the 7B scale, and SVD+QK fine-tuning of Mistral-7B. The results show that when (d_select = d_model/4), the method can achieve approximately 75% Key cache savings and around 37.5% overall KV cache savings. For existing models, substantial Key cache compression can be achieved with only a small amount of QK fine-tuning, at a quality degradation of about 2%.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf8 \cb3 \strokec8 Reasons To Accept:
\f1\b0 \cf7 \cb1 \strokec7 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf7 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec7 The method is simple and transferable. It can be applied by performing truncated SVD on the existing (W_K), without requiring retraining from scratch.\cb1 \
\ls6\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec7 The experiments are relatively comprehensive, covering different models and tasks.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf8 \cb3 \strokec8 Reasons To Reject:
\f1\b0 \cf7 \cb1 \strokec7 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa30\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf7 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec7 The experimental design of this paper is flawed. The KV cache memory bottleneck, as well as the main motivation of the paper, targets long-context inference scenarios. However, the experiments include relatively few evaluations that directly assess long-context capabilities. The paper mainly reports conventional tasks such as PPL, HellaSwag, ARC, WinoGrande, MMLU, and GSM8K. Therefore, the experiments do not truly substantiate the paper\'92s main claim.\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec7 A natural baseline for this work is Multi-head Latent Attention. The authors do include a comparison in Table 16, but this comparison is insufficient, as it lacks complete empirical measurements under the same training setup and the same inference system.\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec7 The paper repeatedly uses terms such as \'93syntactic roles,\'94 \'93semantic clusters,\'94 and \'93positional patterns,\'94 but does not provide precise definitions for these concepts.\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec7 In fact, using different key/value dimensionalities is already a common design choice in some existing models, especially those based on MLA architectures. For example, DeepSeek-V3 uses different key and value dimensionalities. This raises concerns about the novelty of the paper\'92s findings.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf8 \cb3 \strokec8 Rating:
\f1\b0 \cf7 \strokec7 \'a04: Ok but not good enough - rejection\cb1 \

